# MORE HAUS — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development, and set the same values on the host for
# production.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MAKING THE FORMS WORK — do one of these two. Until you do, the contact form
# and the newsletter signup are written to the server log and reach nobody.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OPTION 1 — email (simplest; one key and you are live)
#
#   1. Make an account at resend.com and create an API key.
#   2. Paste it below and set the address the studio reads.
#
# Inquiries arrive as email with reply-to set to whoever wrote in, so answering
# is just hitting reply.
RESEND_API_KEY=
INQUIRY_TO_EMAIL=

# Optional. Until you verify a domain with Resend, leave this blank and their
# shared sending address is used, which works immediately. Once morehaus.com is
# verified, set something like "MORE HAUS <studio@morehaus.com>".
INQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL=

# OPTION 2 — send the submissions somewhere else instead
#
# Each is POSTed as JSON. Point them at a form service (Formspark, Basin), an
# automation hook (Zapier, Make), a CRM, or a mailing list provider (Flodesk,
# Mailchimp, Klaviyo). Only used when RESEND_API_KEY is empty.
INQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=
NEWSLETTER_WEBHOOK_URL=
